    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Spec point** — `spcpt_YNMDJhymrSm5ZT8k`",
    "reading_order" : 2,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000003",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Thermal Stability",
    "reading_order" : 3,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 2,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000004",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Thermal decomposition **is the breakdown of a compound into two or more different substances using **heat**",
    "reading_order" : 4,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000005",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Thermal decomposition of carbonates",
    "reading_order" : 5,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000006",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "In Group 1, lithium carbonate when heated will decompose producing lithium oxide and carbon dioxide",
    "reading_order" : 6,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000007",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Li**<sub>**2**</sub>**CO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$**  Li**<sub>**2**</sub>**O (s)  +  CO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g)**",
    "reading_order" : 7,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000008",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The rest of the Group 1 carbonates don't decompose at Bunsen temperatures",
    "reading_order" : 8,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000009",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The decomposition temperatures increase as you go down the Group",
    "reading_order" : 9,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000010",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The Group 2 carbonates break down (**decompose**) when they are heated to form the **metal oxide **and give off **carbon dioxide gas**",
    "reading_order" : 10,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The general equation for the decomposition of Group 2 carbonates is:",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**XCO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$** XO (s) + CO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g)**",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**X = Group 2 element**",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Going **down **the group, more heat is needed to break down the carbonates",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000015",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**MgCO**<sub>**3**</sub>** **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$** MgO + CO**<sub>**2**</sub>",
    "reading_order" : 15,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Thermal decomposition of nitrates",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000017",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The only Group 1 nitrate that will decompose to produce nitrogen dioxide (which is a brown toxic gas) and oxygen is lithium nitrate LiNO<sub>3</sub>",
    "reading_order" : 17,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000018",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**4LiNO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$** 2Li**<sub>**2**</sub>**O (s) + 4NO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g) + O**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g)**",
    "reading_order" : 18,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000019",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The rest of the Group don't decompose so completely producing the metal** nitrite** (NO<sub>2</sub><sup>-</sup>) and oxygen, but no nitrogen dioxide",
    "reading_order" : 19,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000020",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**2XNO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$** 2XNO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (s) + O**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g)**",
    "reading_order" : 20,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000021",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "All the nitrates from sodium to caesium decompose in this same way, the only difference being how hot they have to be to undergo the reaction.",
    "reading_order" : 21,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000022",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Down Group 1, the decomposition gets more difficult, and you have to use higher temperatures.",
    "reading_order" : 22,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000023",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The Group 2 nitrates break **decomposed** when they are heated to form the **metal oxide,** **oxygen gas** and **nitrogen dioxide gas**",
    "reading_order" : 23,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000024",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Since the formed nitrogen dioxide gas is toxic, the decomposition of nitrates is often carried out in a **fume cupboard**",
    "reading_order" : 24,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000025",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The general equation for the decomposition of Group 2 nitrates is:",
    "reading_order" : 25,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000026",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Mg(NO**<sub>**3**</sub>**)**<sub>**2**</sub>**  **$\\overset{\\mathrm{HEAT}}{\\rightarrow}$** MgO + **$\\frac{1}{2}$**O**<sub>**2**</sub>** + 2NO**<sub>**2**</sub>",
    "reading_order" : 26,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000027",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**X = Group 2 element**",
    "reading_order" : 27,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000028",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Going **down **Groups 1 and 2, more heat is needed to break down the carbonate and nitrate ions",
    "reading_order" : 28,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000029",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The thermal stability of the Group 1 and 2 carbonates and nitrates therefore **increases** down the group",
    "reading_order" : 29,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000030",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The smaller positive ions at the top of the groups will polarise the anions more than the larger ions at the bottom of the group",
    "reading_order" : 30,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000031",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The small positive ion attracts the delocalised electrons in the nitrate or carbonate ion towards itself",
    "reading_order" : 31,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000032",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The higher the charge and the smaller the ion the higher the polarising power",
    "reading_order" : 32,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000033",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The more polarised they are, the more likely they are to thermally decompose as the bonds in the carbonate and nitrate ions become weaker",
    "reading_order" : 33,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000034",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Testing for gases",
    "reading_order" : 34,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000035",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Carbon dioxide",
    "reading_order" : 35,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000036",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "When bubbled through limewater, carbon dioxide gas will turn the limewater milky",
    "reading_order" : 36,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000037",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This is a fine white precipitate of calcium carbonate, CaCO<sub>3</sub>",
    "reading_order" : 37,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000038",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Ca(OH)**<sub>**2 **</sub>**(aq) + CO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g) → CaCO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) + H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O (l)**",
    "reading_order" : 38,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000039",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Oxygen",
    "reading_order" : 39,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000040",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "If oxygen gas is present, it will relight a glowing splint",
    "reading_order" : 40,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000041",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**C (s) + O**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g) → CO**<sub>**2 **</sub>**(g) **",
    "reading_order" : 41,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000042",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Nitrogen dioxide",
    "reading_order" : 42,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
